Did the script run okay without a cleanup? The 139 probably means it's not even loading.

On a new cluster, i test using hadoop streaming:

hadoop dfs -rmr /user/sguha/Rfolder-release.tar.gz ; hadoop dfs -put Rfolder-release.tar.gz /user/sguha/ ;hadoop dfs -rmr /user/sguha/tmp/goo.txt ; hadoop jar /usr/lib/hadoop/contrib/streaming/hadoop-streaming-0.20.2-cdh3u2.jar -Dmapred.reduce.tasks=0 -Dmapred.map.tasks=0 -archives "hdfs://admin4.generic.metrics.scl3.mozilla.com/user/sguha/Rfolder-release.tar.gz#Rfolder-release <http://admin4.generic.metrics.scl3.mozilla.com/user/sguha/Rfolder-release.tar.gz#Rfolder-release>" -input /user/sguha/tmp/foo.txt  -output /user/sguha/tmp/goo.txt -mapper runme.sh -file /home/sguha/runme.sh

foo.txt is some lines
and runme.sh is

cd Rfolder-release/Rdist 1>&2
exec ./mscript.sh

By modifying  mscript.sh, i can detect if the libraries are being loaded successfully (look at the attempt log files from the TT nodes).

Yes, it's not perfect. Not sure of a good design to fix this.

Regards
Saptarshi

