That's right, I oversaw it. The mapred.cache.archive has it as #Rfolder.
My test Rscript is working now.

Another detail i oversaw and corrected is in mscript.sh I had
"export Rex=$bin/R/bin/R-temp" instead of "export Rex=$bin/R/bin/R-$RANDOM"
This was driven by desire to simplify things but resulted in strange behavior - some tasks attempts were failing intermittently with "subprocess failed with code 139" but sometime there was correct output produced by single map! I found your comment
"Observe how the R/bin/R executable is written to a randomly named file. This is because this script will be called simultaneously by the JVMs on the node"
Could you explain why is it important? In R+Hadoop one can create an archive from R, ship it to the nodes, substitute parameters in R, and there is no need to produce multiple instances of R executable. Why Rhipe is different?

Thanks for all help and quick responses! This is very helpful.
I should be doing more experiments and will send my comments later (if they will be helpful)

--Konstantin

