"Observe how the R/bin/R executable is written to a randomly named file. This is because this script will be called simultaneously by the JVMs on the node"
Could you explain why is it important? In R+Hadoop one can create an archive from R, ship it to the nodes, substitute parameters in R, and there is no need to produce multiple instances of R executable. Why Rhipe is different?

R+Hadoop invokes the R executable. RHIPE has

In the R script you'll see

#!/bin/sh
# Shell wrapper for R executable.

R_HOME_DIR=/home/sguha/lib64/R
if test "${R_HOME_DIR}" = "/home/sguha/lib64/R"; then
   case "linux-gnu" in

(replace with your directory of installation), since R is now being invoked from the remote nodes, R_HOME needs to be changed.
and therefore the sed script to a random filename.

I'm working on some experiments to see if this can be changed e.g. just invoke R and execute a package

